attack_data.tsv, written.tsv: the main values of every entry of the logs
in tests/fixtures/attack_data/ (Splunk's open samples) and
tests/fixtures/written/ (written for these tests), one line per entry: the
file, the line, the vendor, the kind, the time, the action, source, source
port, destination, destination port, protocol, user, application, rule,
device and message. Written by gen.py, which reads the files with Python's
own csv and re modules, after the vendors' documentation (PAN-OS 11.1's
field orders, FortiOS's log keys, the ASA's message wording), with no code
shared with this crate; see its header.

Regenerate from the crate's root:

  python3 -I tests/oracle/gen.py tests/fixtures/attack_data > tests/oracle/attack_data.tsv
  python3 -I tests/oracle/gen.py tests/fixtures/written > tests/oracle/written.tsv

tests/oracle.rs compares every entry with them.
